<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Padua</h1><p class="st-meta">1318 CE – 1405 CE · capital Padua</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Carrara lordship of Padua, patrons of Petrarch and rivals of Venice, whose last lords were strangled in a Venetian prison.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Threatened by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cangrande-i-della-scala">Cangrande della Scala</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-padua">Commune of Padua</a> in 1318 elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacopo-i-da-carrara">Jacopo I da Carrara</a> as its lord. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carraresi">Carrara</a> lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-verona">Lordship of Verona</a> from 1328 to 1337 but then returned, ruling as hereditary lords.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carraresi">Carraresi</a> governed from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggia-carrarese">Reggia Carrarese</a> palace and controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua's</a> university, which flourished. Francesco I, called the Elder, ruled from 1350, welcomed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrarch">Petrarch</a> and expanded the state towards <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-treviso">Treviso</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a>, making him a rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giusto-de-menabuoi">Giusto de' Menabuoi</a> frescoed the baptistery for the family. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-galeazzo-visconti">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-padua">Padua</a> in 1388, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-novello-da-carrara">Francesco Novello</a> regained it in 1390.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After a long war, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a> captured <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-padua">Padua</a> in 1405. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-novello-da-carrara">Francesco Novello</a> and two of his sons were strangled in prison in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1406, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> remained Venetian until 1797.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1318 CE – 1405 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.93%;width:1.73%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1318 CE – 1405 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Padua</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jacopo I da Carrara, Francesco I da Carrara, Francesco II Novello da Carrara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Venetian, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Carrara lordship, Carraresi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1362&amp;focus=lordship-of-padua" aria-label="Lordship of Padua on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4962 576 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Padua lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5282 832L5282 832M5282 832L5293 831"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5282 832h0M5293 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5282 832h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5282 832h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Padua. <a href="/atlas?year=1362&amp;focus=lordship-of-padua">On th